  "definition": "A wallet address is a public, shareable identifier on a blockchain network to which assets can be sent and from which ownership is asserted. It is typically derived deterministically from a public key by hashing and encoding, allowing anyone to send funds to it while only the holder of the corresponding private key can authorise outgoing transactions. Addresses are network-specific in format and serve as the destination in transactions and the anchor for on-chain balance accounting.",
